STATUTORY CORPORATION
Limitations of Statutory Corporation
☑Theoretical Autonomy: The autonomy and flexibility of such
enterprises exist on paper only. In reality, a statutory corporation is
subject to many rules and regulations and does not enjoy as much
operational flexibility in its working.
Government Interference: The working of public corporations is
subject to interference from buregucrats and politicians, especially
in case of major decisions or where huge funds are involved.
Undesirable Practices: In statuary corporations, officials may
misuse their autonomy and indulge in unfair practices (like
corruption), that are against the objectives of such enterprises.
