Limitations of Statutory Corporation
☑Delay in Action: Government often appoints advisors to
the Corporation Board. It adversely affects the freedom
in entering into contracts and other decisions.
Rigid Structure: The objectives, powers and functions of
statutory corporations are prescribed by the Act and
these can be changed only by amending the Act, which
is quite time consuming and complicated.
